questions.problem:
Two players – Andriy and Olesya play the following game. On a table, there is a rounded cake, which is cut by one of them into $4n$ different in weight sectors (pieces). Weight of every part is known by each player. After that they choose pieces for themselves upon following rules. At first Andriy chooses 1 piece, then Olesya chooses 2 pieces, but so that the pieces, that are left after her turn, form a sector. Then they take in turns 2 pieces, so that after every step pieces that are on the table form a sector. Making the last step Andriy takes the last piece. Each player aims that the total weight of the part of the cake, he or she took, is bigger, than opponent's one. Is it possible that someone surely takes more than half of the whole cake if:
a) Olesya cuts the cake into sectors;
b) Andriy cuts the cake into sectors, but at his first step he is prohibited to take the biggest on weight piece?

